WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:02.760
In 1955, the philosopher J.

2
00:00:02.810 --> 00:00:02.960
L.

3
00:00:03.010 --> 00:00:06.310
Mackie set three beliefs side by side.

4
00:00:06.360 --> 00:00:08.030
God is omnipotent.

5
00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.950
God is wholly good.

6
00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:11.730
Evil exists.

7
00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:16.470
Mackie claims that these three cannot all
be held together without contradiction.

8
00:00:16.520 --> 00:00:20.510
In the exam, an excerpt of his
argument is printed in front of you.

9
00:00:20.560 --> 00:00:23.930
How do you take it apart
in about 45 minutes?

10
00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.650
In this mission, you'll
rebuild Mackie's triangle,

11
00:00:26.700 --> 00:00:30.430
and meet the replies he
calls fallacious solutions.

12
00:00:30.480 --> 00:00:33.730
Then you'll see Alvin Plantinga
answer him on free will,

13
00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.410
and turn that clash into a paragraph.

14
00:00:36.460 --> 00:00:40.090
Your mission: find out how to
take a printed argument apart,

15
00:00:40.140 --> 00:00:41.170
against the clock.
